# 必考词 Unit26
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2025红宝书考研英语词汇
# 描述: 必考词Unit26核心词汇

{{identify}}{{/aɪˈdentɪfaɪ}}{{v. 识别； identify；确认}}{{The police identified the suspect from the footage.}}
{{identity}}{{/aɪˈdentəti}}{{n. 身份； identity；特性}}{{The company has a strong brand identity.}}
{{ignorant}}{{/ˈɪɡnərənt}}{{adj. 无知的； ignorant；不了解的}}{{He was ignorant of the risks involved.}}
{{ignore}}{{/ɪɡˈnɔːr}}{{v. 忽视； ignore；不理睬}}{{You should not ignore the warning signs.}}
{{illustrate}}{{/ˈɪləstreɪt}}{{v. 说明； illustrate；画插图}}{{The diagram illustrates the process clearly.}}
{{image}}{{/ˈɪmɪdʒ}}{{n. 形象； image；图像}}{{The company is trying to improve its public image.}}
{{immediate}}{{/ɪˈmiːdiət}}{{adj. 立即的； immediate；直接的}}{{The problem requires immediate attention.}}
{{immense}}{{/ɪˈmens}}{{adj. 巨大的； immense；无限的}}{{The project requires an immense amount of work.}}
{{immune}}{{/ɪˈmjuːn}}{{adj. 免疫的； immune；不受影响的}}{{Some people are immune to the disease.}}
{{impact}}{{/ˈɪmpækt}}{{n./v. 影响； impact；冲击}}{{The policy had a significant impact on education.}}
{{implement}}{{/ˈɪmplɪment}}{{v./n. 实施； implement；工具}}{{The government implemented new regulations.}}
{{implication}}{{/ˌɪmplɪˈkeɪʃn}}{{n. 含义； implication；暗示}}{{The findings have important implications for policy.}}
{{implicit}}{{/ɪmˈplɪsɪt}}{{adj. 含蓄的； implicit；无疑问的}}{{There was an implicit agreement between them.}}
{{imply}}{{/ɪmˈplaɪ}}{{v. 暗示； imply；意味着}}{{His silence implied consent.}}
{{import}}{{/ɪmˈpɔːt}}{{v./n. 进口； import；输入}}{{The country imports oil from the Middle East.}}
{{impose}}{{/ɪmˈpəʊz}}{{v. 施加； impose；强制实行}}{{The government imposed a ban on smoking in public.}}
{{impress}}{{/ɪmˈpres}}{{v. 使印象深刻； impress；铭刻}}{{Her performance impressed the judges.}}
{{impulse}}{{/ˈɪmpʌls}}{{n. 冲动； impulse；脉冲}}{{She bought the dress on impulse.}}
{{incentive}}{{/ɪnˈsentɪv}}{{n. 激励； incentive；刺激}}{{The company offers financial incentives to employees.}}
{{incident}}{{/ˈɪnsɪdənt}}{{n. 事件； incident；事故}}{{The incident was reported to the police.}}
{{incline}}{{/ɪnˈklaɪn}}{{v./n. 倾向； incline；斜面}}{{I am inclined to agree with you.}}
{{incorporate}}{{/ɪnˈkɔːpəreɪt}}{{v. 合并； incorporate；包含}}{{The new design incorporates the latest technology.}}
{{incredible}}{{/ɪnˈkredəbl}}{{adj. 难以置信的； incredible；惊人的}}{{The view from the top was incredible.}}
{{incur}}{{/ɪnˈkɜːr}}{{v. 招致； incur；引起}}{{The company incurred heavy losses.}}
{{indicate}}{{/ˈɪndɪkeɪt}}{{v. 表明； indicate；指示}}{{The data indicates a growing trend.}}
{{individual}}{{/ˌɪndɪˈvɪdʒuəl}}{{adj./n. 个人的； individual；个体}}{{Each individual has unique talents.}}
{{induce}}{{/ɪnˈdjuːs}}{{v. 引起； induce；劝诱}}{{Stress can induce health problems.}}
{{industry}}{{/ˈɪndəstri}}{{n. 工业； industry；行业}}{{The tourism industry is important to the economy.}}
{{inevitable}}{{/ɪnˈevɪtəbl}}{{adj. 不可避免的； inevitable}}{{Change is inevitable in life.}}
{{infant}}{{/ˈɪnfənt}}{{n./adj. 婴儿； infant；初期的}}{{The infant was sleeping peacefully.}}
{{inflation}}{{/ɪnˈfleɪʃn}}{{n. 通货膨胀； inflation}}{{Inflation has risen to 5% this year.}}
{{influence}}{{/ˈɪnfluəns}}{{n./v. 影响； influence；权势}}{{Social media has a great influence on young people.}}
{{inform}}{{/ɪnˈfɔːm}}{{v. 通知； inform；了解}}{{Please inform us of any changes.}}
{{infrastructure}}{{/ˈɪnfrəstrʌktʃər}}{{n. 基础设施； infrastructure}}{{The country needs to invest in infrastructure.}}
{{ingredient}}{{/ɪnˈɡriːdiənt}}{{n. 成分； ingredient；因素}}{{Fresh ingredients make the food taste better.}}
{{inhabit}}{{/ɪnˈhæbɪt}}{{v. 居住于； inhabit}}{{Many species inhabit the rainforest.}}
{{initial}}{{/ɪˈnɪʃl}}{{adj./n. 最初的； initial；首字母}}{{The initial results are very promising.}}
{{initiate}}{{/ɪˈnɪʃieɪt}}{{v. 发起； initiate；开始}}{{The company initiated a new project.}}
{{innocent}}{{/ˈɪnəsnt}}{{adj. 无辜的； innocent；天真的}}{{The jury found him innocent.}}
{{innovation}}{{/ˌɪnəˈveɪʃn}}{{n. 创新； innovation}}{{Innovation is the key to success.}}
{{input}}{{/ˈɪnpʊt}}{{n. 投入； input；输入}}{{We need more input from the team.}}
{{inquiry}}{{/ɪnˈkwaɪəri}}{{n. 调查； inquiry；询问}}{{The police launched an inquiry into the incident.}}
{{insert}}{{/ɪnˈsɜːt}}{{v./n. 插入； insert；插页}}{{Please insert the key into the lock.}}
{{insight}}{{/ˈɪnsaɪt}}{{n. 洞察力； insight；见解}}{{The book provides valuable insights into human behavior.}}
{{inspect}}{{/ɪnˈspekt}}{{v. 检查； inspect；视察}}{{Health inspectors inspected the restaurant.}}
{{inspire}}{{/ɪnˈspaɪər}}{{v. 激励； inspire；启发}}{{Her speech inspired many young people.}}
{{install}}{{/ɪnˈstɔːl}}{{v. 安装； install；就职}}{{They installed a new air conditioning system.}}
{{instance}}{{/ˈɪnstəns}}{{n. 实例； instance；场合}}{{For instance, you could try a different approach.}}
{{instinct}}{{/ˈɪnstɪŋkt}}{{n. 本能； instinct；直觉}}{{Animals rely on instinct to survive.}}
{{institute}}{{/ˈɪnstɪtjuːt}}{{n./v. 学院； institute；建立}}{{The research institute published a new study.}}
{{institution}}{{/ˌɪnstɪˈtjuːʃn}}{{n. 机构； institution；制度}}{{The institution has a long history.}}
{{instruct}}{{/ɪnˈstrʌkt}}{{v. 指导； instruct；命令}}{{The teacher instructed the students to open their books.}}
{{instrument}}{{/ˈɪnstrəmənt}}{{n. 仪器； instrument；乐器}}{{The laboratory is equipped with modern instruments.}}
{{insufficient}}{{/ˌɪnsəˈfɪʃnt}}{{adj. 不足的； insufficient}}{{The evidence is insufficient to support the claim.}}
{{insure}}{{/ɪnˈʃʊər}}{{v. 给…保险； insure；确保}}{{You should insure your house against fire.}}
{{integrate}}{{/ˈɪntɪɡreɪt}}{{v. 整合； integrate；融入}}{{The company integrated the new software into its system.}}
{{intellectual}}{{/ˌɪntəˈlektʃuəl}}{{adj./n. 智力的； intellectual；知识分子}}{{The university is a center of intellectual activity.}}
{{intelligence}}{{/ɪnˈtelɪdʒəns}}{{n. 智力； intelligence；情报}}{{Artificial intelligence is changing many industries.}}
{{intend}}{{/ɪnˈtend}}{{v. 打算； intend；意指}}{{I intend to finish the report by Friday.}}
{{intense}}{{/ɪnˈtens}}{{adj. 强烈的； intense；紧张的}}{{The competition was very intense.}}
{{interact}}{{/ˌɪntərˈækt}}{{v. 互动； interact；相互作用}}{{Children learn by interacting with each other.}}
{{interpret}}{{/ɪnˈtɜːprɪt}}{{v. 解释； interpret；口译}}{{The data can be interpreted in different ways.}}
{{intervene}}{{/ˌɪntəˈviːn}}{{v. 干预； intervene；介入}}{{The government intervened to stabilize the economy.}}
{{intimate}}{{/ˈɪntɪmət}}{{adj. 亲密的； intimate；私人的}}{{They have been intimate friends for years.}}
{{investigate}}{{/ɪnˈvestɪɡeɪt}}{{v. 调查； investigate；研究}}{{The police are investigating the robbery.}}
{{invest}}{{/ɪnˈvest}}{{v. 投资； invest；投入}}{{She invested heavily in the stock market.}}
{{invisible}}{{/ɪnˈvɪzəbl}}{{adj. 看不见的； invisible；无形的}}{{The bacteria are invisible to the naked eye.}}
{{involve}}{{/ɪnˈvɒlv}}{{v. 涉及； involve；使参与}}{{The project involves many different departments.}}
{{isolate}}{{/ˈaɪsəleɪt}}{{v. 隔离； isolate；孤立}}{{The patient was isolated to prevent the spread of infection.}}
{{issue}}{{/ˈɪʃuː}}{{n./v. 问题； issue；发行；发布}}{{Climate change is an important issue.}}
{{justify}}{{/ˈdʒʌstɪfaɪ}}{{v. 证明…正当； justify；辩护}}{{How can you justify the expense?}}
{{keen}}{{/kiːn}}{{adj. 热衷的； keen；敏锐的}}{{She is keen on learning new languages.}}
{{laboratory}}{{/ləˈbɒrətɔːri}}{{n. 实验室； laboratory}}{{The experiment was conducted in the laboratory.}}
{{landscape}}{{/ˈlændskeɪp}}{{n. 风景； landscape；形势}}{{The landscape of education is changing rapidly.}}
{{launch}}{{/lɔːntʃ}}{{v./n. 发射； launch；推出}}{{The company launched a new product line.}}
{{layer}}{{/ˈleɪər}}{{n. 层； layer；层次}}{{The atmosphere has several layers.}}
{{leadership}}{{/ˈliːdəʃɪp}}{{n. 领导力； leadership；领导层}}{{Good leadership is essential for success.}}
{{lean}}{{/liːn}}{{v./adj. 倾斜； lean；精益的}}{{The company adopted a lean management approach.}}
{{legislation}}{{/ˌledʒɪsˈleɪʃn}}{{n. 立法； legislation；法律}}{{The government passed new environmental legislation.}}
{{legitimate}}{{/lɪˈdʒɪtɪmət}}{{adj. 合法的； legitimate；正当的}}{{The claim is legitimate and well-supported.}}
{{leisure}}{{/ˈleʒər}}{{n. 休闲； leisure；空闲}}{{Leisure activities are important for mental health.}}
{{liberal}}{{/ˈlɪbərəl}}{{adj. 自由的； liberal；开明的}}{{She has liberal views on social issues.}}
{{liberate}}{{/ˈlɪbəreɪt}}{{v. 解放； liberate；释放}}{{The city was liberated after months of occupation.}}
{{license}}{{/ˈlaɪsns}}{{n. 许可证； license；执照}}{{You need a license to practice medicine.}}
{{likewise}}{{/ˈlaɪkwaɪz}}{{adv. 同样地； likewise；也}}{{He is a talented musician, and likewise a great teacher.}}
{{limit}}{{/ˈlɪmɪt}}{{n./v. 限制； limit；限度}}{{There is a time limit for the exam.}}
{{link}}{{/lɪŋk}}{{n./v. 链接； link；联系}}{{The study links diet to heart disease.}}
{{literacy}}{{/ˈlɪtərəsi}}{{n. 识字； literacy；读写能力}}{{The program aims to improve adult literacy.}}
{{literally}}{{/ˈlɪtərəli}}{{adv. 字面上； literally；确实}}{{He literally ran all the way home.}}
{{literary}}{{/ˈlɪtərəri}}{{adj. 文学的； literary；书面的}}{{She won a prestigious literary award.}}
{{literature}}{{/ˈlɪtrətʃər}}{{n. 文学； literature；文献}}{{She studied English literature at university.}}
{{locate}}{{/ləʊˈkeɪt}}{{v. 位于； locate；定位}}{{The hotel is located in the city center.}}
{{logical}}{{/ˈlɒdʒɪkl}}{{adj. 逻辑的； logical；合理的}}{{Your argument is logical and convincing.}}
{{loom}}{{/luːm}}{{v./n. 隐约出现； loom；织布机}}{{A crisis looms on the horizon.}}
{{maintain}}{{/meɪnˈteɪn}}{{v. 维持； maintain；保养}}{{It is important to maintain a healthy lifestyle.}}
{{major}}{{/ˈmeɪdʒər}}{{adj./n. 主要的； major；专业}}{{She chose physics as her major.}}
{{majority}}{{/məˈdʒɒrəti}}{{n. 多数； majority；成年}}{{The majority of people support the proposal.}}
{{manage}}{{/ˈmænɪdʒ}}{{v. 管理； manage；设法}}{{She manages a team of 20 people.}}
{{manifest}}{{/ˈmænɪfest}}{{v./adj. 表明； manifest；明显的}}{{The symptoms manifested themselves early.}}
{{manipulate}}{{/məˈnɪpjuleɪt}}{{v. 操纵； manipulate；操作}}{{He tried to manipulate the election results.}}
{{manner}}{{/ˈmænər}}{{n. 方式； manner；礼貌}}{{She spoke in a friendly manner.}}
{{manual}}{{/ˈmænjuəl}}{{adj./n. 手工的； manual；手册}}{{Please read the instruction manual carefully.}}
{{manufacture}}{{/ˌmænjuˈfæktʃər}}{{v./n. 制造； manufacture；制造业}}{{The company manufactures electronic components.}}
{{margin}}{{/ˈmɑːdʒɪn}}{{n. 边缘； margin；利润；余地}}{{The company operates on a narrow profit margin.}}
{{mass}}{{/mæs}}{{n./adj. 大量； mass；大规模的}}{{A mass of people gathered in the square.}}
{{massive}}{{/ˈmæsɪv}}{{adj. 巨大的； massive；大规模的}}{{The project requires a massive investment.}}
{{mature}}{{/məˈtʃʊər}}{{adj./v. 成熟的； mature；使成熟}}{{He is mature enough to make his own decisions.}}
